"### Regulatory arbitrage \u2014 the RWA wedge Coinbase & Robinhood can't copy\n\nHyperliquid's builder dexes are already trading **~$782.45M/day** of tokenised equities, indices and commodities (NVDA, SP500, GOLD, TSLA, even OPENAI/SPACEX pre-IPO) \u2014 **permissionlessly and non-custodially**. That is precisely what a US-licensed venue *structurally cannot* offer:\n\n- **Coinbase / Robinhood** hold custody & broker-dealer licenses \u2192 offering a permissionless S&P 500 perp would collide with securities law and their own compliance perimeter (counter-positioning).\n- **Hyperliquid** is offshore + non-custodial + geoblocks the US \u2192 it operates in the regulatory gap, so it can list an equity perp in a day where a broker needs quarters of legal review.\n\n**Two ways to read this (both true):**\n- \ud83d\udfe2 *Bull / moat:* reg-arb is a durable structural edge \u2014 the faster global-macro-on-chain venue wins users a licensed app can't serve. Widening product breadth diversifies HYPE's cash flows beyond crypto beta.\n- \ud83d\udd34 *Tail risk:* the same arbitrage is the **single biggest regulatory target**. Offering equity/index exposure invites SEC/CFTC (and CME/ICE-lobbied) scrutiny; geoblocking \u2260 immunity. See Regulatory Outlook.\n\n<sub>Builder-dex volume live from Hyperliquid `perpDexs` + per-dex ctxs. Competitor rows are curated facts; fees approximate and vary by tier/pair.</sub>"